From 672a1f92ff4a57815d2430acd6cf733edbc44791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 14:02:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add app-wide micro-interactions: press feedback, skeletons,
 transitions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce a shared src/ui/kit.js with reusable primitives (ProgressBar,
Skeleton, ConfettiBurst, LoadingScreen) and global keyframes injected
once at startup, then apply them across the client-facing screens:

- All buttons get a global :active press-scale/brightness feedback.
- Root loading screens (App, ClientView, WorkoutView) use a breathing
  logo / skeleton placeholders instead of static "Kraunama..." text.
- The 5 tab overlays (WorkoutView, BookingClient, ProgressPhotos,
  TrainingPackages, ClientStats) fade/slide in on open instead of
  popping in instantly.
- WorkoutView: checkmarks pop in on completion, exercise progress bar
  gets a gradient/glow, empty "no plan" state has a breathing emoji,
  and finishing all exercises triggers a brief confetti burst.
- TrainingPackages: active package credit bar uses the same
  gradient/glow progress bar style.
- StepsTracker: save button now transitions smoothly between its
  enabled/disabled states.

FoodLog.js and RecipeSuggestion.js were left untouched — neither is
imported/reachable from the app, so they're dead code.
